QuickCap Voice Agent – Functional Flow Document

Version: v1
Source: Converted from QuickCap IVR User Guide → Conversational Voice Agent
Target Stack:

Twilio Voice (call handling)

Vocode (voice orchestration)

Deepgram (STT)

ElevenLabs (TTS)

OpenAI LLM (dialog + reasoning)

Backend APIs (Claims / Auth / Eligibility)

1. Overview

This document defines the complete conversational voice flow to replace the legacy DTMF IVR with a human-like conversational AI agent.

The agent must:

Greet caller

Understand natural language

Ask for required information

Validate inputs

Call backend APIs

Read results conversationally

Offer repeat / restart / transfer options

Handle corrections and retries

The bot replaces the IVR menu but preserves ALL original business logic and decision paths.

2. Call Entry Flow
2.1 Call Start

When a call is received:

Agent says:

"Thank you for calling. I can help you check claim status, authorization status, or member eligibility. How can I assist you today?"

Intent Classification

LLM must classify user intent into:

Intent	Example Utterances
CLAIM_STATUS	"check claim", "claim status", "payment for claim"
AUTH_STATUS	"authorization", "pre approval", "auth status"
ELIGIBILITY	"is member covered", "eligibility", "coverage"
UNKNOWN	anything else

If UNKNOWN → go to fallback flow.

3. Shared Conversational Rules
3.1 Universal Input Rules

For every collected input:

Ask for value

Repeat value back

Ask confirmation

If incorrect → re-ask

Retry policy:

Max retries per field: 3

After 3 failures → transfer to customer service.

3.2 Confirmation Template

After any input:

"You said {value}. Is that correct?"

If user says:

Yes → continue

No → ask again

