5. CLAIM STATUS FLOW
5.1 Data Required
Field	Format
Member ID	numeric only
DOB	MM/DD/YYYY
Service Date	MM/DD/YYYY
Caller Type	Patient / Provider
NPI/Tax ID	only if Provider
5.2 Step-by-Step Conversation
Step 1 — Member ID

Agent:

"Please provide the member ID. Numbers only."

Validate numeric.

Confirm.

Step 2 — Date of Birth

Agent:

"Please provide the member’s date of birth."

Confirm.

Step 3 — Service Date

Agent:

"Please provide the claim service date."

Confirm.

Step 4 — Caller Type Branch

Agent:

"Are you the patient or a provider?"

Intent classification:

Patient

Provider

5.3 PATIENT PATH

Call backend:

GET /claims?memberId&dob&serviceDate

Multiple claims handling

If multiple claims returned:

Read each claim sequentially

IMPORTANT:
Patient path does NOT require NPI or Tax ID. 

IVR User Guide (3) (1) (1)

5.4 PROVIDER PATH

Ask:

"Please provide the NPI or Tax ID associated with the claim."

Confirm → call API.

GET /claims?memberId&dob&serviceDate&npiTaxId

5.5 Deliver Results

Agent summarizes:

Claim status

Payment status

Dates

Amounts

5.6 Post-Result Menu (Claim Flow)

Agent must offer options:

Voice Option	Action
Repeat	Repeat information
Another claim	Restart claim flow
Main menu	Go to main
Not what I need	Transfer to customer service

This exactly mirrors IVR post-options. 

IVR User Guide (3) (1) (1)

6. AUTHORIZATION STATUS FLOW
6.1 Data Required
Field	Required
Member ID	Yes
DOB	Yes
Caller Type	Patient/Provider
NPI/Tax ID	Only for Provider
6.2 Steps
Step 1 — Member ID
Step 2 — DOB

(same validation pattern)

Step 3 — Caller Type Branch

Agent:

"Are you calling as the patient or a provider?"

6.3 PATIENT AUTH PATH

Call:

GET /authorizations?memberId&dob

If single authorization:

Read authorization number + details.

If multiple authorizations:

Agent must present options:

"I found multiple authorizations. Please choose by requested date."

User selects date → fetch specific authorization.

This branch is critical from IVR doc. 

IVR User Guide (3) (1) (1)

6.4 PROVIDER AUTH PATH

Ask:

"Please provide the NPI or Tax ID of the referring provider."

Call:

GET /authorizations?memberId&dob&npiTaxId


Same multiple/single logic as patient.

6.5 Post-Result Menu (Authorization)

Options identical to claims:

Repeat

Another authorization

Main menu

Transfer to customer service

7. ELIGIBILITY FLOW
7.1 Data Required
Field	Required
Member ID	Yes
DOB	Yes
7.2 Steps

Ask Member ID

Confirm

Ask DOB

Confirm

Call API:

GET /eligibility?memberId&dob


Return:

Coverage status

Plan details

Effective dates

7.3 Post-Result Menu (Eligibility)

Offer:

Voice Option	Action
Repeat	Repeat
Another member	Restart eligibility
Main menu	Go to main
Not helpful	Transfer
8. FALLBACK & ERROR HANDLING
8.1 Unknown Intent

"I’m sorry, I can help with claim status, authorization status, or eligibility. Which would you like?"

3 failures → transfer.

8.2 No Records Found

Agent:

"I couldn’t find any records with the information provided."

Offer:

Retry

Customer service

8.3 Transfer to Customer Service

Triggered when:

User asks for agent

Too many retries

User presses fallback options

Twilio transfer:

<Redirect to customer service number>

9. Conversation UX Requirements

The agent must:

Speak naturally

Use conversational confirmations

Allow interruptions

Allow corrections anytime

Allow “start over”

Allow “go back”

